26,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
27,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
28,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It's worse than I thought. People are shifting bikes to get out, and some spots are completely exposed to rain.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Our building account is nearly empty. Also, the local ward park is expensive and has a long waiting list, so we can't rely on it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,George,,My suspicions were right. The same flats have held the best spots for years without any review. Daily riders are open to paying.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,Be careful with fees. The neighbors tried that and it just created resentment and caused people to stop attending meetings.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The paperwork is already a pain! Adding more billing would be a nightmare, and those fancy racks look hard to use and maintain.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@George, if the same people always have the dry spots, that explains the tension. We need a system that's fair and efficient.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I see the risk, but we have no funds for improvements. A paid system could actually build a reserve for the building.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,George,,"@Asuka, exactly. The current ""first-come, first-served"" from years ago isn't working for the new residents.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, money often ruins neighborly relations. If we can't find a way to avoid conflict, we're just trading one problem for another.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, if we get new racks, who is going to grease them? I don't want one person stuck with all the work again.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, that's why a simple rotation or a clear rule is better than complex hardware.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, if we charge a fee, perhaps we can pay a service or a resident to handle the maintenance.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,George,,"A lottery might be the most neutral way to break the old patterns, though it's random.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"A lottery is clean. No one can complain about the ""system"" being biased, only about their luck.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Mio,,"As long as it doesn't require a mountain of monthly paperwork, I'm open to it!","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Asuka,,We need to consider the daily riders who are willing to pay for stability.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"If we go with a paid model, it solves the funding issue and the allocation issue simultaneously.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,George,,I'm leaning toward something that disrupts the current stagnation.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I still worry about the social cost of payments, but a lottery is a safe middle ground.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Mio,,I'm just worried about the workload. Let's see the options.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
