55,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option B sounds like it would increase the ""shoving match"" and damage bikes. I prefer C for fairness.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option A is the most rational. It generates revenue for the building and reflects the value of the spaces.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,George,,"Option A appeals to the daily riders, but Option C finally ends the legacy of the same people holding the best spots.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is a recipe for the same social breakdown the neighbors had. I vote for C.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option B sounds like a maintenance nightmare with those racks. Option A is too much paperwork. I'll go with C!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the social friction from payments might outweigh the financial gain.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the current friction from the ""shoving match"" is already a cost. A paid system is transparent.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, I agree it's transparent, but a lottery is the most ""gentle"" way to reset the status quo.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,Exactly. C is the only one that doesn't introduce a new source of resentment.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Mio,,"Yeah, a once-a-year draw is way easier to manage than monthly billing!","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I agree with Mio. C is the most sustainable for the community.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I still believe A is the most efficient, but I see the consensus forming around C.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,George,,I'll support C. It's fair and solves the stagnation problem.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,It seems we have a winner.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Mio,,Yay! Let's do the lottery!,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
